  "id": "Solar_Plan_Farm",
  "stac_version": "1.1.0",
  "description": "<img width=\"25%\" src=\"https://gtif-ukif.github.io/gtif-ukif-client/assets/ucl-logo.webp\">\n\nThis indicator allows you to define a rectangular area (using the usual shift-click and expand right down or up) for planning the location of a new solar farm. By default, the Overlay layers will switch on the Open Infrastructure Map, and the Environmentally Sensitive Regions (Natural Landscapes, National Parks and Sites of Special Scientific Interest) as well as the LWM (Land Water mask). In the data layers switch on the BFG (Bi-Facial Gain) and only for England switch on the VOM canopy height. For other areas, switch on the Meta-CHM although you should be aware that the heights here are biase high compared with the VOM. This will allow you to ensure that your solar farm will not intersect any tree shadow. You can also switch on the Total productivity if you preferentially want to look at regions with low productivity.",
